  <section|Exact endpoint and external hypotheses><label|exact-endpoint-and-external-hypotheses>

  <verbatim|YangMills.jointExistence> in <verbatim|Lean/Solution.lean> proves
  <verbatim|YangMills.JointExistence>, defined in
  <verbatim|Lean/ChallengeSpec.lean>. Its sole explicit input is a
  <verbatim|YangMills.GaugeGroup> with <verbatim|GaugeGroup.IsSimple>.
  <verbatim|Lean/PublicTheory.lean> makes this a closed subgroup of a
  specified finite-dimensional unitary matrix group, together with the real
  subspace of matrices whose every real exponential lies in the subgroup. The
  <verbatim|generates> equivalence ties that subspace to the group; it is not
  an arbitrary Lie algebra. <verbatim|IsSimple> explicitly requires a nonzero
  commutator and no nontrivial proper real ideal. Connectedness of the group
  is not a separate hypothesis.

  The precise quantifier order is: for each such group, one Wilson family C;
  regularity of C; for every strictly increasing volume-index map p, a
  strictly increasing q and a hierarchy T for C satisfying the four
  properties along p composed with q. C precedes p. The hierarchy and
  refinement may depend on p, but are chosen before arity, observable, test,
  OPE configuration, and truncation. The theorem does not assert equality or
  uniqueness of the hierarchies chosen for different p.

  The proof takes the internal penalty b equal to 1. The more general
  <verbatim|YangMills.constructed> accepts arbitrary b \<gtr\> 0; this
  penalty is neither an additional hypothesis of <verbatim|jointExistence>
  nor the public bare coupling. The public regularity predicate only requests
  some positive logarithmic running slope. <verbatim|YangMills.regular> in
  <verbatim|Lean/HierarchyBridge.lean> supplies the particular slope
  <verbatim|2 * YM.Pert.Asymptotics.b0 g.core>.

  <section|Meaning-determining checks><label|meaning-determining-checks>

  <\enumerate>
    <item><strong|Wilson origin and limits.> <verbatim|YangMills.wilsonLaw>,
    <verbatim|WilsonFamily.finiteMoment>, and <verbatim|WilsonFamily.smear>
    in <verbatim|Lean/PublicWilson.lean> use the normalized exponential of
    the actual plaquette action against product Haar measure, followed by
    products of insertions and mesh-weighted lattice sums.
    <verbatim|WilsonRegularity> requires continuity, gauge invariance and a
    token-dependent finite lattice-offset stencil uniform in cutoff, volume
    and anchor. <verbatim|WilsonFamily.Converges> requires the full mesh
    sequence to converge on every suitable fixed-volume row. A further
    increasing volume subsequence converges to the unselected hierarchy
    tested off collision diagonals. This is not a diagonal-only convergence
    assertion and is not convergence to the selected phase.

    <item><strong|Public insertion scope.> The public token type and
    insertion functions are existential data. The public predicate does not
    separately identify tokens with predetermined Wilson loops or curvature
    polynomials, and the grade-four field in the public trace test is not
    defined there as a stress-tensor trace. This is a limit on what can be
    read from the public statement, not evidence that the constructed
    observables are arbitrary. In fact <verbatim|YangMills.wilsonFamily> uses
    <verbatim|YM.Family.seen>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Source/Construction.lean>
    defines these through calibrated local sections and transfer data, and
    proves <verbatim|Family.translation>, <verbatim|reality>,
    <verbatim|constant>, <verbatim|invariant>, <verbatim|localO>, and
    <verbatim|continuousO>. Any stronger physical identification in the
    article must explain these definitions or use a separately justified
    internal result.

    <item><strong|Wightman content.> <verbatim|Lean/PublicTheory.lean>
    contains actual common-domain operators, a normalized dense cyclic vacuum
    domain, continuity in Schwartz tests, the smeared adjoint identity,
    spacelike commutativity, a strongly continuous unitary translation
    action, and a projection-valued energy-momentum measure with its
    characteristic-function relation to translations. W0 requires support in
    the closed forward cone and uniqueness of translation-invariant vectors
    up to the vacuum. W2 fixes the ordinary affine test pullback and full
    proper orthochronous Poincare coordinates; it is not covariance under an
    unspecified trivial symmetry group. Reconstruction additionally requires
    faithful nonzero fields, injectivity of each finite-dimensional
    field-space map, coverage of all labels, and surjectivity of token
    projection. These inspected clauses rule out the immediate
    empty-label/all-zero-field reading. No positive gap is required.

    <item><strong|Analytic bridge.> <verbatim|Hierarchy.Reconstructed> states
    holomorphy in the complex time coordinates for each fixed collection of
    spatial coordinates, on strictly ordered imaginary times. It identifies
    the selected Euclidean correlations at purely imaginary times and the
    boundary limits after smearing against products of Schwartz tests. It
    does not state a general full complex-spacetime tube theorem in this
    public interface. Permutation symmetry and smoothness concern separated
    configurations. The phase space is compact metrizable, with a probability
    measure of full support and correlations continuous in the phase;
    integration gives the unselected correlations.

    <item><strong|OPE quantifiers.> <verbatim|Hierarchy.OperatorProductExpansion>
    uses one coefficient system for every phase and every truncation. The
    coefficient threshold can depend on labels, degree, channel and geometric
    constants. For fixed labels and truncation, the remainder threshold
    precedes all admissible positions and all phases. The finite cluster is
    contained in a ball of radius Mr and has pairwise separation at least eta
    r; spectators are separated from each other and the center by c. There is
    no threshold uniform over every truncation degree or every field label.
    Both full and shortened words are evaluations of this same hierarchy.

    <item><strong|Trace test.> The selected two-point function of a centered
    degree-four field satisfies the precise nonzero asymptotic <verbatim|r^8
    log^2(1/r) T_2(r) -\<gtr\> 3 dim_R(g.lieAlgebra)/pi^4>. The excluded
    comparison class consists of finite sums of finite products of the
    explicitly defined mass-shell kernels, including the stated differential
    numerators. Exclusion of all generalized free fields is not this
    conclusion. Internal <verbatim|YM.Nonperturbative.Headline.TraceExclusions>
    additionally contains the physical centered stress-trace identity and
    conditional Maxwell comparisons. Those stronger clauses must not be
    silently attributed to the four-field public property record.
  </enumerate>

  <section|What the inspected proof establishes, and where the main work
  lies><label|what-the-inspected-proof-establishes-and-where-the-main-work-lies>

  The endpoint proof is a short specialization and projection, faithfully
  preserving the common witness. In <verbatim|Lean/Construction.lean>,
  <verbatim|YangMills.constructed> obtains one internal witness from
  <verbatim|YM.Nonperturbative.existence> and combines <verbatim|regular>,
  <verbatim|wilsonLimit>, <verbatim|publicReconstruction>,
  <verbatim|publicOPE>, and <verbatim|publicTrace>. The corresponding bridge
  files actually identify the lattice law, field system, continuation and
  word evaluations; they do not create an unrelated public witness.

  The next layer is also assembly: <verbatim|YM.Nonperturbative.continuum_with_position_tests>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/Nonperturbative/Continuum.lean> consumes
  <verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun> and
  <verbatim|YM.R2IGoals.fromFunded>. The latter's <verbatim|Broad.refine> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/R2I/Campaign/Accepted.lean> already supplies full-mesh
  ordered convergence, a <verbatim|Spec.Final>, every-phase reconstruction, a
  trace result, and OPE inputs. In particular <verbatim|Spec.Final> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Spec/Closed.lean> already contains contours, a Wightman
  system and its realization. Assuming a Final and then proving W0\UW3 by
  unpacking its fields is a valid interface lemma, but is not a
  reconstruction proof from the lattice.

  Minimum substantive obligations for a complete article, beyond the public
  bridge, are:

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Obligation>>|<cell|<strong|What
  must actually be supplied>>|<cell|<strong|Inspected source interface
  locating it>>>|<row|<cell|One calibrated family>|<cell|Construct the common
  running trajectory, local calibrated observables and all quantitative
  estimates needed later, before choosing extraction orders.
  Finite-dimensional compactness of each lattice alone does not provide
  uniform estimates.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun>;
  <verbatim|YM.Family.Makes>; funded-run selection called in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>>>|<row|<cell|Continuum
  extraction>|<cell|Prove simultaneous correlation control, full mesh
  convergence on suitable rows, volume extraction, smooth separated limits,
  and retention of the relevant positivity and symmetry estimates.
  Subsequence compactness alone cannot replace full mesh
  convergence.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.R2IGoals.fromFunded>,
  <verbatim|Broad.refine>, <verbatim|Spec.Seed>; <verbatim|from_spec> with
  <verbatim|hJ.fullMesh>>>|<row|<cell|Fields and phase
  selection>|<cell|Construct physical quotient spaces, compatible inclusions,
  nontriviality, phase space and measure, the selected character, and the
  common phase mixture identities.>|<cell|<verbatim|Spec.Algebra>,
  <verbatim|Locals>, <verbatim|Materializes>, <verbatim|Final>;
  <verbatim|HierarchyBridge.publicReconstruction>>>|<row|<cell|Relativistic
  reconstruction>|<cell|Supply the analytic continuation and boundary
  estimates, positivity/quotient Hilbert space, common invariant domain and
  tempered fields, Poincare action, spectrum, locality and uniqueness of the
  invariant vacuum. Verify hypotheses of any reconstruction theorem
  cited.>|<cell|<verbatim|Spec.Relativistic>;
  <verbatim|YM.Boundary.Wightman.Realizes> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Fields/System.lean>; <verbatim|EveryPhase.Completed> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/EveryPhase/Extension.lean>>>|<row|<cell|OPE>|<cell|Construct
  the same coefficients/fields and prove the coefficient and phase-uniform
  remainder estimates for every fixed truncation, with the specified
  spectator geometry.>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Independent.Core>,
  <verbatim|YM.OPE.Orbits.Foundation>, <verbatim|Headline.SeparatedOPE>>>|<row|<cell|Trace>|<cell|Identify
  the chosen degree-four observable if a physical stress-trace claim is made;
  prove its centering and exact logarithmic asymptotic; prove the stated
  comparison-class exclusion.>|<cell|<verbatim|Headline.TraceExclusions>;
  <verbatim|YangMills.publicTrace> in <verbatim|Lean/TraceBridge.lean>>>>>>

  These are mathematical inputs to an assembly exposition, not extra
  assumptions of the formal endpoint. An article may state them as
  outstanding inputs while drafting, but cannot call the resulting
  conditional assembly a complete proof of existence. Contacts, nested OPE,
  all-character Wightman theories and leading perturbative position tests are
  stronger retained results; determine whether to prove them as necessary
  internal steps or omit their separate conclusions from the existence
  article.

  <section|Evidence and limits><label|evidence-and-limits>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Read the repository contribution, coordination and proof-standard
    documents; the issue and all current comments;
    <verbatim|source/README.md>, relevant <verbatim|source/audit.md>
    sections, <verbatim|source/evidence/axioms-3456e5e.md>, the
    public-statement ledger, <verbatim|Bots/README.md>, and shared background
    index. The shared background directory currently provides an SU(2)
    simplicity note, not a verified reconstruction/construction reference for
    these obligations. No new literature theorem is invoked or certified by
    this report.

    <item>Independently read the actual pinned source files named above,
    beginning with <verbatim|Solution.lean>, <verbatim|ChallengeSpec.lean>,
    <verbatim|PublicTheory.lean>, and <verbatim|PublicWilson.lean>, then the
    construction and bridge definitions and immediate assembly inputs. Used
    <verbatim|cat>, bounded <verbatim|sed> and <verbatim|rg>; a search for
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Spec/Final.lean> failed because the definition is in
    <verbatim|Spec/Closed.lean>, which was then read. No source files were
    edited.

    <item><verbatim|git rev-parse HEAD> returned the clone base recorded
    above; starting <verbatim|git status --short> was empty.

    <item><verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was run after
    creating this report and failed because the new unit's
    <verbatim|unit.json> is not present in the review-only clone. That file
    belongs to the parent's integration output; the checker must be rerun
    after integration. <verbatim|git diff --check> passed separately. Neither
    command validates the mathematical findings.

    <item>Existing versioned evidence reports only <verbatim|propext>,
    <verbatim|Classical.choice>, and <verbatim|Quot.sound> for the endpoint
    and successful kernel replay of its audited closure from a
    checksum-verified prebuilt artifact. This report reuses that evidence and
    does not claim to have rerun it. No full rebuild, axiom audit,
    independent kernel implementation, or Lean scratch proof was run here.

    <item>This is a targeted interface audit, not a transitive semantic audit
    of the RG construction or a proof that its public predicates meet every
    conventional physical meaning of \PYang-Mills existence.\Q There is no
    justified finding of a false or vacuous endpoint from this inspection.
    There is also no basis here for certifying the complete human-readable
    proof.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Required drafting safeguards><label|required-drafting-safeguards>

  Preserve the stated quantifier order and the distinction between unselected
  limits and selected reconstruction. Label every undischarged substantive
  input visibly. Do not infer reconstruction, full mesh convergence, OPE or
  trace asymptotics from finite Wilson normalization and regularity alone.
  Give an independent draft review after the actual manuscript files and
  their complete dependency ledger are available. Human acceptance remains
  outstanding.

